+# CSV import
+
+## What and why
+
+Sales keeps leads in spreadsheets and wants to load a whole CSV file into contactbook
+instead of adding contacts one by one. `import_contacts` reads a CSV file with the same
+columns as our export (`name,email,phone,tags`) — or `first_name,last_name` instead of
+`name`, as written by the address-book export script — creates new contacts, updates
+existing ones, and returns an **import report** saying what happened per row.
+
+## Interface (fixed — other code calls exactly this)
+
+- `src/contactbook/importer.py`: `import_contacts(repo: InMemoryContactRepository, data: str | bytes) -> ImportReport`
+  where `data` is the file content: raw bytes as read from disk, or already-decoded text.
+- `ImportReport` (dataclass, same module): `created: list[str]`, `updated: list[str]` (normalised
+  emails), `errors: list[RowIssue]`, `warnings: list[RowIssue]`.
+- `RowIssue` (dataclass, same module): `row: int`, `column: str | None`, `message: str`.
+- `ImportFileError(ContactError)` in `src/contactbook/errors.py`, raised when the file as a whole
+  can't be imported.
+
+`import_contacts`, `ImportReport`, `RowIssue` and `ImportFileError` are also exported from
+`contactbook`.
+
+## Rules
+
+### File level
+
+- Bytes are decoded as UTF-8; a leading UTF-8 BOM is stripped. No other encodings.
+  Undecodable bytes → `ImportFileError` whose message tells the user to re-save the file
+  as "CSV UTF-8".
+- Text input starting with the BOM character (U+FEFF) has it stripped too.
+- Delimiter is comma only. Standard CSV quoting (as written by `export_csv` / Excel).
+- Row 1 is the header. Header names are matched trimmed and case-insensitively; column
+  order is free.
+- Required: an `email` column, and either a `name` column or both `first_name` and
+  `last_name`. Otherwise → `ImportFileError`. `phone` and `tags` are optional.
+- If `name` is present, it is used and `first_name`/`last_name` are treated as unknown.
+- Unknown header columns → one warning each (`row=1`, `column=None`), never an error.
+  Blank header cells are ignored silently (values under them: see "Per row").
+- Row 1 blank while later rows are not → `ImportFileError` saying row 1 must be the header.
+- A column the import uses appearing twice in the header → `ImportFileError`. Unused
+  columns (including `first_name`/`last_name` next to `name`) only warn, even if repeated.
+- Empty file (no content, or only blank lines) → `ImportFileError`.
+- Header-only file → empty report, no error.
+- More than **1000** contact rows (blank rows not counted) → `ImportFileError`, nothing imported.
+- Malformed CSV the parser rejects (strict quoting) → `ImportFileError` naming the line.
+- Whenever `ImportFileError` is raised, the repository is unchanged.
+
+### Row numbering
+
+- `RowIssue.row` is the row number as Excel shows it: header is row 1, first data row is
+  row 2, blank lines count. A quoted cell spanning several lines is still one row.
+
+### Per row
+
+- **Blank rows** (no cells, only commas, or only whitespace) are skipped silently.
+- **Email** is the identity: normalised with `normalize_email`. Missing/invalid → error,
+  column `email`. `created` / `updated` list normalised emails, in file order.
+- **Name** is required on every row, including updates; validated with `validate_name`.
+  With `first_name`/`last_name`, name = `first_name + " " + last_name`, then validated.
+  Problems → error, column `name` (also in a first/last-name file).
+- **Tags**: cell split on `;`, empty pieces ignored, each piece normalised with
+  `normalize_tag`, repeats collapse. Any invalid tag → error on the whole row, column `tags`.
+- **Phone**: blank cell or missing column → phone not touched. Non-blank and invalid
+  (per `normalize_phone`) → **warning**, column `phone`; the rest of the row is still
+  applied and the phone stays as it was (none for a new contact).
+- A row with any error is **not applied at all**, not even partly. All of the row's errors
+  are reported (one `RowIssue` per failing column).
+- **Duplicate email within the file**: the first row that is applied with that email wins;
+  a later row with the same email is an error on the later row, column `email`,
+  message `duplicate of row N`. A rejected row does not claim its email.
+- Non-blank values beyond the header's width or under a blank header cell → one warning
+  per row (`column=None`); those values are ignored. Missing trailing cells count as blank.
+- Warnings (phone, extra values) are also reported on rows that have errors, so the user
+  can fix a row in one pass.
+
+### Create vs update
+
+- Email not in the repo → **create** the contact; listed in `created`.
+- Email in the repo → **update**:
+  - name: replaced by the file value;
+  - phone: replaced only if the cell has a valid value; blank never clears it;
+  - tags: union of existing and file tags; an import never removes tags.
+  - Listed in `updated` only if the stored contact actually changed.
+- Import is **partial**: valid rows are applied, rows with errors are skipped and reported.
+
+`column` values in issues are always lower-case: `name`, `email`, `phone`, `tags`, or `None`.
+
+## Acceptance criteria (each is a test in `tests/test_importer.py`)
+
+- [ ] Output of `export_csv` imports back into an empty repo unchanged (round trip).
+- [ ] Bytes with and without UTF-8 BOM, and text with a leading U+FEFF, import the same.
+- [ ] Non-UTF-8 bytes → `ImportFileError` mentioning "CSV UTF-8"; repo unchanged.
+- [ ] Empty file / blank-lines-only file → `ImportFileError`.
+- [ ] Missing `email` header, or no `name` and not both `first_name`/`last_name` → `ImportFileError`.
+- [ ] Header-only file → empty report.
+- [ ] Header matched case-insensitively with surrounding spaces, any column order.
+- [ ] `first_name`/`last_name` columns build the name; name problems there report column `name`.
+- [ ] Unknown column → warning on row 1, import proceeds.
+- [ ] 1000 contact rows (plus blank rows) import; 1001 → `ImportFileError`, repo unchanged.
+- [ ] Row numbers: header row 1, first data row 2, blank lines counted, multi-line cells count once.
+- [ ] Blank, comma-only and whitespace-only rows skipped without issues.
+- [ ] Invalid / missing email → error with column `email`; row not applied.
+- [ ] Missing name → error with column `name`, also when updating an existing contact.
+- [ ] Invalid tag → error with column `tags`; an existing contact is left untouched.
+- [ ] Invalid phone → warning with column `phone`; contact created without phone / existing phone kept.
+- [ ] Update replaces name, keeps phone on blank cell or missing column, replaces it on a value, unions tags.
+- [ ] Unchanged existing contact is not listed in `updated`.
+- [ ] Duplicate email in file → later row error `duplicate of row N`; first row applied.
+- [ ] A row whose first occurrence was rejected can still be applied later in the file.
+- [ ] `created`/`updated` contain normalised emails.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Other encodings (cp1252, UTF-16), delimiter sniffing, `;`-separated files.
+- Removing tags or clearing phones via import.
+- Deleting contacts not present in the file.
+- Dry-run / preview mode; all-or-nothing transactions.
+- Streaming very large files (the 1000-row cap makes this unnecessary).
+
+## Scope limits
+
+- New module `src/contactbook/importer.py`, `ImportFileError` in `errors.py`, exports in
+  `__init__.py`, tests in `tests/test_importer.py`. Standard library only.
+- No changes to validation, model, repository or export behaviour.
